qas=[('Why use Suricata labels?','They enabled deterministic large-scale weak supervision, but they are not treated as perfect ground truth. The thesis explicitly limits the claim to alert-associated behaviour.'),('Why a two-stage model instead of end-to-end training?','Freezing Stage 1 isolates intra-flow representation from Stage 2 context and makes ablations easier to attribute. End-to-end optimisation is future work.'),('Is Stage 2 truly causal?','It is causal in stable flow-start order and excludes future items and labels. It is not strict streaming availability causality because earlier long-lived flows may not have completed.'),('Why is source-host context best?','It is the strongest observed relation for this capture, plausibly because repeated outbound activity preserves scanning or retry patterns. Binary labels cannot prove the mechanism.'),('Why macro-F1 and average precision?','The positive prevalence is low. Macro-F1 weights both classes equally, while average precision focuses on ranking the positive class.'),('Can the results generalise?','External tests show useful transfer to CICIDS2017 windows and another server, but performance varies. The evidence is preliminary rather than universal.')]
